  "acrm---key-feature-4-content": "<h3>A filled PDF of every application</h3><p>Each online application can be kept as a filled PDF in the same layout for the personnel file, typed signature included. Name each file by applicant and role, like Haddad_RN.pdf.</p>",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Job Application Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a job application form?\", \"a\": \"A job application form is the record a candidate fills out to apply for a specific opening, usually before any interview. Employers covered by federal EEOC rules keep every application for at least one year, including those from people they never hired.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a job application form online?\", \"a\": \"Describe the role in a few sentences, and Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> turns them into an online job application form with resume uploads and an applicant table. To reword a question or add a role, ask in plain English, and the change goes live on the same link.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a job application form for employment include?\", \"a\": \"Most forms use six sections. Applicant details: name, address, phone, email, work authorization. Position: role, pay, start date, hours. Work history, per job: employer, title, dates, reason for leaving, \\\"May we contact this employer?\\\" Then education, references and a signed, dated certification.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between an application form and a resume?\", \"a\": \"A resume is the candidate's own summary, in whatever layout they choose. An application form asks every candidate the same questions in the same order, including details a resume often leaves out, such as work authorization, availability, and a signed statement that the answers are true. Many employers ask for both and collect the resume as an upload on the form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a job application form template I can start from?\", \"a\": \"Start from the six sections above, or from your own. If HR has a fillable job application form template it likes, paste its questions into the prompt and the rebuilt form keeps that wording and order. Applicants who know the paper version then find familiar questions online, and managers read answers where they expect them.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is an application for employment form the same as a job application form?\", \"a\": \"They are the same document. Some employers print the longer title at the top of the page, but the questions underneath do not change.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a simple job application form look like?\", \"a\": \"A simple job application form asks only what decides a first call. For an hourly role that means contact details and availability, then the most recent job and one reference. Limit the blank PDF to one past job and one reference and it fits on a single letter page, certification included.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an employee application form used for?\", \"a\": \"An employee application form is used to decide whom to interview and hire. It sets each candidate's work history and work authorization side by side in one format. Payroll and emergency contact details come after the offer, on a new employee form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do I need separate job application forms for each role?\", \"a\": \"Usually not. Separate copies per role tend to drift: the cashier form gets a new availability question and the stock clerk form never does. One form that branches by position changes a shared question once for every role, and each role keeps its own extra questions.\"}, {\"q\": \"What happens after someone submits an online job application form?\", \"a\": \"The applicant can get a confirmation email right away, and the application waits in its first stage for review. Moving someone to a closed stage can send a short decline. Shortlisted applicants can receive a candidate screening form with scored questions.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}